From: LG6851F MT6990 maintenance <local@lg6851f>
Date: Wed, 26 Aug 2026 20:18:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt76: mt7996: reject short MCU events

mt7996_mcu_rx_event() reads fields from the MCU RX descriptor before checking
that the skb contains a complete descriptor. Reject and consume truncated
events before dispatching them to legacy or unified handlers.

Signed-off-by: LG6851F MT6990 maintenance <local@lg6851f>
---
 mt7996/mcu.c | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

--- a/mt7996/mcu.c
+++ b/mt7996/mcu.c
@@ -938,6 +938,11 @@ void mt7996_mcu_rx_event(struct mt7996_d
 {
 	struct mt7996_mcu_rxd *rxd = (struct mt7996_mcu_rxd *)skb->data;
 
+	if (skb->len < sizeof(*rxd)) {
+		dev_kfree_skb(skb);
+		return;
+	}
+
 	if (rxd->option & MCU_UNI_CMD_UNSOLICITED_EVENT) {
 		mt7996_mcu_uni_rx_unsolicited_event(dev, skb);
 		return;
